  "text": "Professor Tim Bentley | Our people | University of Liverpool\nSkip to main content\nSelect campus:\nUK\nChina\nIndia\nOnline\nHome\nMenu\nMenu\nStudy\nOpen\nStudy\nmenu\nStudent life\nOpen\nStudent life\nmenu\nResearch and innovation\nOpen\nResearch and innovation\nmenu\nGlobal\nOpen\nGlobal\nmenu\nAbout us\nOpen\nAbout us\nmenu\nClose\nBack\nStudy\nView all courses\nUndergraduate\nPostgraduate taught\nPostgraduate research\nContinuing education\nContinuing professional development\nOnline learning\nInternational\nGlobal opportunities\nXJTLU\nThe XJTLU partnership\nPaying for your studies\nTuition fees\nScholarships and bursaries\nLoans and grants\nGraduation\nWidening participation\nVisit us\nOpen days\nCampus tours\nOnline events\nVirtual tour\nContact us\nTerm dates and semesters\nClose\nBack\nStudent life\nLife on campus\nFacilities\nLibrary\nStudy areas\nFood and drink\nEvents\nLife in Liverpool\nWhy choose Liverpool?\nGetting to Liverpool\nGetting around Liverpool\nAccommodation\nFind accommodation\nLife in halls\nGuild of Students\nSport at Liverpool\nStudent support\nMental health and wellbeing\nVisas and immigration\nBook an appointment\nLiverpool Advantage\nCareers\nWelcome week\nMoney advice\nManaging your money\nClose\nBack\nResearch and innovation\nResearch frontiers\nAI for life\nInfection resilience\nMaterials discovery\nParticle physics\nTherapeutics innovation\nInterdisciplinary Centre for Sustainability Research\nExplore our research\nFind a research unit\nOur research community\nFacilities and equipment\nOur impact\nResearch outputs\nResearch excellence framework (REF)\nCollaboration: innovation and growth\nOur partners\nInnovation assets and capabilities\nKnowledge Exchange Framework (KEF)\nContact us\nPostgraduate research\nDoctoral Training\nFellowships\nResearch environment\nResearcher support\nResearch news\nOriginal Ideas podcast\nClose\nBack\nGlobal Liverpool\nPartnerships\nStrategic partners\nGlobal networks\nTransnational education partners\nCollaborate with us\nGlobal study opportunities\nStudy abroad\nStudy in Liverpool\nStudy in China\nStudy in India\nAchievements and rankings\nOur global city\nSustainability\nOur global team\nLeadership team\nGlobal contacts\nOur global community\nClose\nBack\nAbout us\nThe University\nOur history\nStrategy and vision\nPeople and culture\nRankings and reputation\nReports, policies and governance documents\nOur structure\nWork at Liverpool\nOur city, our inspiration\nDiscover Liverpool\nOur commitment to the Liverpool City Region\nProfessional Services\nIT Services\nHuman Resources\nLegal\nOur campus\nCampus facilities\nLibraries\nSports facilities\nSustainability\nEquality, diversity and inclusion\nNews\nEvents\nLiverpool Literary Festival\nHire an event space\nVisit us\nMuseums and Collections\nCar parking\nContact us\nNews\nJobs\nDonate\nA-Z\nAlumni\nStaff\nStudents\nSearch the site\nOur people\nClose\nSearch\nFind courses, people, research, information and more.\nPlease ignore\nWhat types of page to search?\nAll\nCourses\nAcademic staff\nNews\nEvents\nSearch\nPopular pages:\nUndergraduate\nPostgraduate\nPhD\nAccommodation\nResearch\nInternational students\nAlternatively use our\nA-Z index\n.\nhome\nOur people\nProfessor Tim Bentley\nProfessor Tim Bentley\nBVSc (Dist), MRCVS, Veterinary Neurosurgery Certificate, FHEA, DACVIM (Neurology)\nProfessor, Veterinary Neurology & Neurosurgery\nSmall Animal Clinical Science\nPart of\nInstitute of Infection, Veterinary & Ecological Sciences\nFaculty of Health and Life Sciences\nContact\nTim.Bentley@liverpool.ac.uk\nAbout\nResearch\nResearch outputs\nTeaching\nProfessional activities\nAbout\nProfessor Bentley is a board-certified veterinary neurologist-neurosurgeon, and a canine/human brain cancer researcher.\nTim performs translational studies (between canine and human) and translational clinical trials of canine glioma, using spontaneously occurring gliomas in companion animal (pet) dogs as a model for human glioma / glioblastoma.\nHis current translational canine clinical trial is the DOG-FIGhT Trial, developing ferumoxytol (nanoparticle iron) as a radiosensitizer for glioma. In the first arm of the study, dogs diagnosed with glioma receive ferumoxytol pre-operatively, and then surgical biopsies are studied for the impact of ferumoxytol (markers of M1 and M2 subtypes of macrophages, apoptosis, proliferation rate, Prussian blue). Dogs additionally receive post-operative radiation therapy, as an incentive for enrolment.\nTim's previous translational canine glioma clinical trials include metronomic chlorambucil chemotherapy, and post-operative application of genetically-modified oncolytic herpesvirus (M032).\nHe is a founding member of the Comparative Brain Tumor Consortium of the NIH, and a member of the University of Liverpool Brain Cancer research group.\nTim's research involves treating dogs with brain tumours to develop new cures for dogs and people with brain cancer. Donations to his research are used to treat pet dogs with brain tumours AND find new therapies for dogs and people with brain cancer. To donate towards dogs with brain tumours and the cure for canine and human brain cancer, click here! https://www.justgiving.com/campaign/liverpoolcaninebraincancer\nWebsite footer\nInformation for\nCurrent students\nCurrent staff\nProspective students\nBusinesses and partners\nResearchers\nMedia\nStudy at Liverpool\nUndergraduate\nPostgraduate taught\nPostgraduate research\nOnline courses\nCPD\nContinuing education\nInternational students\nQuick links\nJobs at Liverpool\nLibrary\nSport at Liverpool\nFind a researcher\nAlumni\nOur departments and faculties\nAll subjects\nContact us\nUniversity of Liverpool\nFoundation Building\nBrownlow Hill\nLiverpool\nL69 7ZX\nTelephone\n+44 (0) 151 794 2000\nContact us\nMaps and directions\nVisit us\nPart of the\nRussell Group\nAccessibility\nFreedom of information\nCookie information\nData Protection\nModern slavery statement\nTerms and Conditions\nCharitable status\n© University of Liverpool",
